  "question": {
    "text": "A crystalline solid of a pure substance has a face-centred cubic structure with a cell edge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>pm</mi></math> . If the density of the substance in the crystal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> then the number of atoms present in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>256</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of the crystal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>is</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>24</mn></msup></math> . The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Formula of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>For FCC unit cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Edge length,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Number&nbsp;of atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>wt</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>molar</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mass</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>24</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; Hence, the required value of &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
